{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Went out from the people.</b> From the camp to a distant place, intending to find manna there, for they did not trust in El whose spirit they bore." "<b>To gather.</b> This would have been an unequivocal profanation of the Sabbath if they had gathered the thing from its place of growth, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Shabbat 107b): האי מאן דתלש כשותא מהזמי והיני חייב משום תולש — 'one who pulls up hops from the ground is liable for reaping.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase אם לא נאמנה את אל רוחם is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. It may be corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:54.167272848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}